er and she is even  willing to destroy her own simps as we  see the images of destruction all over  to Hart Kingdom the chapter abruptly  switches focus back to the epic battle  between Yami and Dante man I've been  waiting to see what's going on in that  battle for so long and I am definitely  glad that we got to see another glimpse  of it although it was a brief one  hopefully we will get more in the next  chapter from the looks of it Yami has  been attacking Dante and effectively  landing shots on him over and over again  but Dante has just been using that  grotesque flesh regeneration magic to  heal himself interestingly enough even  Dante says that this magic that he has  been using is on  tightly but he admits that he has no  choice but to keep using it because Yami  is just that strong those are definitely  words of high praise from Dante and to  me this really emphasizes the fact that  Yami is on a whole other level from the  other clover mages that we have been  seeing in action so far including of  course William you don't hasta Noel and  so on Yami isn't a whole other League  and he is able to actually offer a real  challenge to Dante as a result of Yami's  impressive strength dante decides to  show Yami the full extent of his demon  power dante is about to use all of the  demonic power that he is capable of  using meaning that he is about to fight  at his absolute strongest Yami responds  by saying that he is about to show Dante  the true power of an ordinary human and  that is how this action-packed chapter  ends both of these epic warriors are  about to get serious they're about to  reveal their final forms and it is going  to be a legendary judging by what we've  seen so far from the dark triad we have  to assume that Dante at full power is  going to be the strongest villain we  have encountered in black colors so far  however we can't count Yami out either  even though as a quote-unquote ordinary  human he is definitely the underdog in  this battle w